    "result_text": "The full suite (the single `AcceptanceTest` class, 2 tests) passes. Done.\n\n## Summary\n\nAdded a derived `locality` field to owners, resolved from a fixed city-to-region table.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`model/CityRegion.java`** (new) \u2014 a small, single-responsibility lookup holding the fixed table (`Sydney\u2192NSW`, `Melbourne\u2192VIC`, `Brisbane\u2192QLD`) with a `CityRegion.of(city)` that returns the canonical region or `\"UNKNOWN\"`. Keeping the table in its own class avoids bloating the entity with a static map.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `@Transient getLocality()` getter that delegates to `CityRegion.of(city)`. This matches the existing derived-field pattern in the codebase (`getInitials`, `getMembershipTier`) \u2014 computed on the fly from stored state, so nothing new is persisted.\n\n3. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 declared `locality` as a read-only string on the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` gets the field; MapStruct then maps `getLocality()` \u2192 `locality` automatically (no mapper change needed).\n\nBoth new acceptance tests (`coreDerivesRegionForKnownCity`, `functionalityUnknownCityIsUnknown`) and the full suite pass green.",
